WEBVTT

00:00:29.792 --> 00:00:32.042
<i>Time to die!</i>

00:00:34.125 --> 00:00:36.958
<i>The perfect world!</i>

00:00:36.958 --> 00:00:44.375
<i>We exchanged promises...</i>

00:00:44.375 --> 00:00:47.083
<i>Let's break the spine!</i>

00:00:47.083 --> 00:00:51.917
<i>...under the moonlight</i>

00:00:51.917 --> 00:00:56.792
<i>At midnight, whispering like a roar</i>

00:00:56.792 --> 00:01:02.208
<i>In the silence and bustle of your current situation</i>

00:01:02.208 --> 00:01:07.417
<i>Do you feel like you're gonna go crazy and break?</i>

00:01:07.417 --> 00:01:11.333
<i>But live your own way, yeah, like you are</i>

00:01:11.333 --> 00:01:15.250
<i>That perfect world!</i>

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:20.458
<i>Let's not be chameleons</i>

00:01:20.458 --> 00:01:25.583
<i>But change ourselves from the inside</i>

00:01:25.583 --> 00:01:29.292
<i>I can hear those words</i>

00:01:29.292 --> 00:01:35.792
<i>Let's shout out so that the</i>
<i>dawn will break all nights</i>

00:01:35.792 --> 00:01:39.500
<i>Gently and furiously</i>

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:51.083
<i>Let's shout out so that the</i>
<i>dawn will rip apart all nights</i>

00:02:02.292 --> 00:02:08.625
We are not available to take your call.
Please leave a message after the tone.

00:02:08.625 --> 00:02:12.417
This is Misato. Where are you, Kisaragi?

00:02:12.417 --> 00:02:13.583
Are you all right?

00:02:15.625 --> 00:02:17.042
"Dark Arts Chapter"

00:02:17.042 --> 00:02:17.958
"Dark Arts Chapter"
"Seventh Night"

00:02:18.458 --> 00:02:19.958
"The Demoniacal Horde"

00:02:22.792 --> 00:02:27.625
Excellent work, Mr. Kisaragi.
Oh my, and who is this?

00:02:27.625 --> 00:02:30.125
This is my grandson, Hisui.

00:02:30.125 --> 00:02:33.125
I brought him along to introduce to you.

00:02:33.125 --> 00:02:34.792
Mother?

00:02:39.042 --> 00:02:40.792
Ah, you're just in time.

00:02:40.792 --> 00:02:43.750
Introduce yourself, Aoi.

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:46.125
Yes, Mother.

00:02:46.125 --> 00:02:49.125
It's nice to meet you. My name is Aoi Misato.

00:02:55.125 --> 00:02:57.125
Aoi!

00:02:57.125 --> 00:02:58.792
Good morning, Aoi!

00:02:58.792 --> 00:03:00.958
Good morning.

00:03:00.958 --> 00:03:04.208
What's the matter? You seem kinda down.

00:03:04.208 --> 00:03:06.750
Oh, no, I'm all right.

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:10.958
Guess it's no surprise even you'd be
depressed at the beginning of the new term.

00:03:10.958 --> 00:03:14.500
And we didn't get to
hang out this summer either.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:17.292
Well, what can you do, right?

00:03:34.208 --> 00:03:35.792
Lady Aoi!

00:03:35.792 --> 00:03:36.833
Yes, ma'am!

00:03:46.458 --> 00:03:48.750
Excellent job, Lady Aoi.

00:03:51.417 --> 00:03:52.500
My...

00:03:56.625 --> 00:04:00.292
Mrs. Misato, I am utterly mortified.

00:04:00.292 --> 00:04:02.000
You clumsy oaf!

00:04:03.167 --> 00:04:07.667
Please, Mr. Kisaragi, it's all right!
Everyone makes mistakes.

00:04:07.667 --> 00:04:12.917
I believe you, yourself have said
that we grow through our mistakes.

00:04:12.917 --> 00:04:18.667
Indeed... Hisui, apologize
once more to Mrs. Misato!

00:04:18.667 --> 00:04:22.125
I'm terribly sorry, Mrs. Misato.

00:04:29.792 --> 00:04:34.125
All right, Misato, translate this part.

00:04:34.125 --> 00:04:36.000
Misato?

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.458
Yes?

00:04:37.458 --> 00:04:41.583
Starting from the sixth line on page 25, please.

00:04:49.708 --> 00:04:51.917
Let's go, Kisaragi!

00:04:57.208 --> 00:04:59.708
What's the matter, Honor Student?

00:04:59.708 --> 00:05:03.750
What's up with staring off into
space and not taking any notes?

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:06.292
You're not as bad as Kyouichi though.

00:05:06.292 --> 00:05:08.417
Well now, here's something
you don't see every day.

00:05:08.417 --> 00:05:12.250
Houraiji and Misato chatting on friendly terms?

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:15.292
Did something happen over summer vacation?

00:05:15.292 --> 00:05:18.333
With a snot-nosed little kid like that?

00:05:18.333 --> 00:05:21.583
Me, I prefer grown-up women actually.

00:05:21.583 --> 00:05:24.708
So, whaddya say, Maria, baby?
Wanna hang with me some time?

00:05:24.708 --> 00:05:28.083
Well, you haven't handed in
your summer homework yet, have you?

00:05:28.083 --> 00:05:29.875
So, how about we "hang" out for
some remedial work after school?

00:05:29.875 --> 00:05:32.125
What? I can't hear you!

00:05:32.125 --> 00:05:33.208
<i>Remedial </i>work.

00:05:33.208 --> 00:05:34.833
Glasses, where are my glasses?

00:05:54.625 --> 00:05:55.792
Fireflies...

00:05:55.792 --> 00:05:59.750
This is my secret place.

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:04.750
One time I got in trouble for
tearing one of my father's scrolls.

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:05.958
Huh?

00:06:05.958 --> 00:06:08.958
I'm the same as you.

00:06:11.292 --> 00:06:12.292
Here.

00:06:42.083 --> 00:06:43.625
Hisui!

00:06:44.958 --> 00:06:47.042
You understand, don't you?

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:57.167
We of the Kisaragi family have served
the Misato family through the ages,

00:06:57.167 --> 00:06:59.792
and have also served to
protect this city of Tokyo

00:06:59.792 --> 00:07:02.667
since as far back as the Edo period.

00:07:02.667 --> 00:07:08.000
I have told you this many times. Isn't that right?

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:09.125
Yes, sir.

00:07:09.125 --> 00:07:14.292
Listen, Hisui, it is about
time that you also learned

00:07:14.292 --> 00:07:19.625
of our family's other mission, which we uphold!

00:08:17.500 --> 00:08:23.125
Kisaragi, I heard about your grandfather.

00:08:28.375 --> 00:08:30.333
You're worried too, huh?

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:35.125
Oh, that's right. We just
received some delicious fruit.

00:08:35.125 --> 00:08:36.750
I'll go get some for you.

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:38.792
You needn't trouble yourself.

00:08:38.792 --> 00:08:40.208
Just wait right there.

00:08:46.208 --> 00:08:47.833
Lady Aoi...

00:08:51.292 --> 00:08:54.083
To think that those creatures have been revived...

00:09:02.625 --> 00:09:06.458
God of Kotoshiro,
God of Naohi, God of Furumita...

00:09:06.458 --> 00:09:11.625
Come now to those who serve
and venerate you at this shrine;

00:09:11.625 --> 00:09:15.083
we implore you, hasten, heal our ills...

00:09:15.083 --> 00:09:18.167
Mirror of the Deep, Mirror of
the Shore, Eight-Hands-Breadth Sword,

00:09:18.167 --> 00:09:21.125
--Jewel of Life, Jewel of Perfection,
--It's cold.

00:09:21.125 --> 00:09:24.458
Jewel of Resurrection,
Jewel of Warding, Snake-Repelling Scarf,

00:09:24.458 --> 00:09:27.417
Bee-Repelling Scarf,
Scarf of Multifarious Protection...

00:09:27.417 --> 00:09:29.125
There we go!

00:09:56.708 --> 00:09:58.542
I've taken it on.

00:09:58.542 --> 00:10:01.750
I've taken on all your resentment!

00:10:01.750 --> 00:10:03.917
What? Kisaragi?

00:10:03.917 --> 00:10:07.750
Yeah, and the shop has had
its shutters closed the whole time.

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:11.083
Sheesh, what the heck is he up to?

00:10:11.083 --> 00:10:13.125
The clouds...

00:10:13.125 --> 00:10:14.292
Huh?

00:10:14.292 --> 00:10:16.792
The clouds look stormy.

00:10:16.792 --> 00:10:19.667
Why, is something <i>troubling </i>you?

00:10:19.667 --> 00:10:21.292
That voice...

00:10:23.625 --> 00:10:27.167
Well, you needn't worry,
now that <i>the </i>Kyouko Tohno is here!

00:10:27.167 --> 00:10:29.167
Look, the latest digital camera!

00:10:29.167 --> 00:10:31.292
--With this, I can--
--Who asked you to come?

00:10:31.292 --> 00:10:32.458
Simply awful!

00:10:32.458 --> 00:10:36.125
Is this any way to treat the newest
member of the Demonbuster Club?!

00:10:36.125 --> 00:10:37.750
Demonbuster Club?

00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:39.042
This ain't no damn school club!

00:10:39.042 --> 00:10:40.458
Hey, who's that?

00:10:40.458 --> 00:10:42.542
Sure not a student from our school, is he?

00:10:42.542 --> 00:10:44.042
Huh? Where?

00:10:44.042 --> 00:10:45.458
Wow, he looks like a model or something!

00:10:45.458 --> 00:10:47.333
What a hunk!

00:10:48.667 --> 00:10:49.750
That's...

00:10:51.292 --> 00:10:53.083
The pot guy!

00:10:54.417 --> 00:10:56.000
Kisaragi!

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:01.458
How does he keep it up?

00:11:05.333 --> 00:11:07.542
These are from Hokkaido.

00:11:11.042 --> 00:11:15.500
Kisaragi, did something happen to you?

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:18.583
Hey! How about saying something?

00:11:20.125 --> 00:11:22.458
Kisaragi, you're wounded.

00:11:22.458 --> 00:11:23.792
Huh?

00:11:23.792 --> 00:11:27.542
What the... You mean you just noticed now?

00:11:27.542 --> 00:11:28.917
Kisaragi...

00:11:28.917 --> 00:11:32.292
You're not gonna tell us
you fell down, now are you?

00:11:36.417 --> 00:11:39.250
I had thought the chain of
strange incidents that occurred here

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:42.333
had been due to some
disturbance in the Dragon Stream,

00:11:42.333 --> 00:11:44.500
but I was wrong.

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:49.000
Someone has made use of the Dark Arts
to deliberately cause these events.

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:50.667
The Dark Arts...

00:11:50.667 --> 00:11:53.792
That crow master guy said
something about that, right?

00:11:55.417 --> 00:11:59.167
"Dark Arts" is a general term to denote sorcery,
which lies in opposition of all that is righteous:

00:11:59.167 --> 00:12:02.333
religion, Heaven, humanity, and the Earth itself.

00:12:02.333 --> 00:12:05.125
There is something known as the Demoniacal Art,

00:12:05.125 --> 00:12:07.625
the path of the demonic,
which is one of the Dark Arts.

00:12:07.625 --> 00:12:10.250
The Demoniacal Art is a dreadful form of sorcery,

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:13.417
which is used to awaken the souls
of the dead and summon demons.

00:12:14.958 --> 00:12:17.792
There was a certain clan
who used the Demoniacal Art

00:12:17.792 --> 00:12:21.000
to incite a rebellion against the Tokugawa
in the last days of the shogunate.

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:24.792
Shogunate? What era was that again?

00:12:24.792 --> 00:12:27.625
The <i>Kurama Tengu </i>era, right?

00:12:27.625 --> 00:12:29.458
<i>Tengu</i>? These aren't demons!

00:12:29.458 --> 00:12:31.958
That's the name of a TV series!

00:12:31.958 --> 00:12:33.917
I don't know their reason for revolting,

00:12:33.917 --> 00:12:37.125
but it is said that this
clan augmented their power

00:12:37.125 --> 00:12:39.000
through the Demoniacal Arts, summoning demons

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:45.000
using the souls of those who died
with a grudge against the Tokugawa.

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:49.458
They called themselves...

00:12:51.708 --> 00:12:53.750
...the Demoniacal Horde.

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:55.833
What?

00:12:55.833 --> 00:12:58.833
It looks like something fun
is about to get underway.

00:13:00.042 --> 00:13:01.667
The Demoniacal Horde...

00:13:01.667 --> 00:13:05.667
The Demoniacal Horde has been revived!

00:13:05.667 --> 00:13:08.167
Now all we need is the Bodhisattva Eye.

00:13:08.167 --> 00:13:10.458
Bodhisattva Eye?

00:13:10.458 --> 00:13:12.792
If the Demoniacal Horde has been revived,

00:13:12.792 --> 00:13:17.042
then it most likely means their
head family, the Kozunu clan, have as well.

00:13:17.042 --> 00:13:18.958
Those guys are the bosses, huh?

00:13:18.958 --> 00:13:20.458
Correct.

00:13:20.458 --> 00:13:25.125
They are trying to wreak havoc
upon this world once again...

00:13:25.125 --> 00:13:27.958
...by using the darkness in people's hearts.

00:13:30.292 --> 00:13:32.458
They're still angry over
the end of the shogunate, huh?

00:13:32.458 --> 00:13:34.292
Talk about a friggin' grudge!

00:13:45.375 --> 00:13:47.708
Kisaragi?

00:13:47.708 --> 00:13:49.042
I...

00:13:50.042 --> 00:13:53.417
I will fight the Demoniacal Horde!

00:13:53.417 --> 00:13:58.083
Because it is my duty as a Kisaragi,

00:13:58.083 --> 00:14:02.625
even if I am alone in that fight,
even if I am left a rotting corpse.

00:14:03.917 --> 00:14:09.083
But you are different.
You have no reason to fight.

00:14:09.083 --> 00:14:12.708
If you feel a need to withdraw from this,
I will not hold it against you.

00:14:12.708 --> 00:14:15.250
It is not too late.

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:17.417
Now that we know it's the
Demoniacal Horde we're up against,

00:14:17.417 --> 00:14:20.083
I cannot guarantee you'll survive this fight.

00:14:20.083 --> 00:14:22.375
Is that okay with you?

00:14:22.375 --> 00:14:25.875
If you are prepared to lay down your life...

00:14:28.208 --> 00:14:30.083
I will fight.

00:14:31.542 --> 00:14:33.250
I will fight.

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:37.792
Me too.

00:14:41.375 --> 00:14:43.000
Komaki!

00:14:43.875 --> 00:14:47.208
What, you're still all worried about that?

00:14:47.208 --> 00:14:48.833
Hey, Doom 'n Gloom...

00:14:48.833 --> 00:14:50.083
What?

00:14:50.083 --> 00:14:54.292
So, basically if we take out all
these Kozunu dudes, that's that, huh?

00:14:54.292 --> 00:14:57.500
Then there won't be any more
people turning into demons, right?

00:14:57.500 --> 00:15:00.083
Yes, that's right.

00:15:00.083 --> 00:15:02.417
Y'hear that, Captain?

00:15:22.083 --> 00:15:24.125
Lady Aoi?

00:15:24.125 --> 00:15:27.000
Is something the matter?

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:29.792
Oh, I'm sorry to be thinking about it now.

00:15:29.792 --> 00:15:33.292
I just remembered something
from a long time ago:

00:15:33.292 --> 00:15:36.458
the time you and I went to see the fireflies.

00:15:43.708 --> 00:15:46.083
It brings back memories.

00:15:46.083 --> 00:15:49.125
Lady Aoi, please forgive me.

00:15:50.125 --> 00:15:55.583
I shall protect you without fail.

00:15:55.583 --> 00:15:57.542
Kisaragi...

00:16:05.917 --> 00:16:07.792
Whoa, this place is...

00:16:07.792 --> 00:16:09.458
Amazing.

00:16:09.458 --> 00:16:11.375
Shady lookin' place.

00:16:11.375 --> 00:16:13.375
These are the sacred
grounds of the Kisaragi family.

00:16:13.375 --> 00:16:15.542
Those who would trespass
upon them shall be cursed.

00:16:15.542 --> 00:16:17.292
Huh?

00:16:17.292 --> 00:16:19.625
Just a silly legend.

00:16:19.625 --> 00:16:23.042
We had reason to make sure
people kept their distance, you see.

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:28.958
Just a silly legend.

00:16:28.958 --> 00:16:30.625
Sorry, you don't sound like him.

00:16:37.125 --> 00:16:38.250
I knew it.

00:16:38.250 --> 00:16:39.917
Kisaragi!

00:16:51.583 --> 00:16:53.458
So, here come those shogunate bastards, huh?

00:16:53.458 --> 00:16:55.292
I knew it, it's the ones from before.

00:16:55.292 --> 00:16:56.958
Those two?

00:16:59.083 --> 00:17:01.125
The Demoniacal Horde...

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:06.083
So, you've finally come. I've been waiting for you.

00:17:07.208 --> 00:17:09.458
The Demoniac Verses...

00:17:09.458 --> 00:17:11.833
It is a volume of dark spells
used to summon demons.

00:17:11.833 --> 00:17:14.583
My clan had sealed it away though.

00:17:14.583 --> 00:17:17.375
Then they stole it, huh?

00:17:17.375 --> 00:17:20.000
And you came here to be sure of it.

00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:23.500
For cryin' out loud, keep your
valuables in a safe or something!

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:25.708
Y'know?

00:17:25.708 --> 00:17:29.167
A barrier like this won't work against me.

00:17:29.167 --> 00:17:33.750
I have thus been able to revive
the Demoniacal Horde without trouble.

00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:37.375
Thank you so much, descendant of the Kisaragi.

00:17:40.292 --> 00:17:43.125
Bastard, tell me your name!

00:17:44.208 --> 00:17:48.667
Kozunu, Tendo Kozunu.

00:17:48.667 --> 00:17:51.750
Tendo Kozunu?

00:17:53.625 --> 00:17:54.958
Kill them.

00:18:16.125 --> 00:18:17.417
Shut the hell up!

00:18:17.417 --> 00:18:19.458
No, this is...

00:18:23.708 --> 00:18:24.958
Aoi!

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:28.583
What? What is this?!

00:18:28.583 --> 00:18:31.167
Stop it!

00:18:33.542 --> 00:18:35.042
Damn...

00:18:45.625 --> 00:18:49.833
Are you my enemy?!

00:18:49.833 --> 00:18:54.292
I, Hisui Kisaragi, shall not
make the same mistake twice!

00:19:08.958 --> 00:19:10.250
Damn!

00:19:11.333 --> 00:19:13.417
Kyouichi!

00:19:13.417 --> 00:19:16.167
Not bad!

00:19:16.167 --> 00:19:18.875
So, tell me, where is it?

00:19:18.875 --> 00:19:22.458
I found the Demoniac Verses easily enough,

00:19:22.458 --> 00:19:25.500
but I've just got no idea where the other thing is.

00:19:25.500 --> 00:19:27.500
C'mon, tell me.

00:19:27.500 --> 00:19:32.042
That's the whole reason
I let you get away before.

00:19:39.750 --> 00:19:43.125
You know what they say,
what goes around comes around.

00:19:43.125 --> 00:19:47.125
Now then, what to do, what to do...

00:19:47.125 --> 00:19:49.125
I've grown weary of you.

00:19:49.125 --> 00:19:54.167
Guess I'll have to kill you all,
and look for it at my own pace.

00:19:55.208 --> 00:19:56.708
Lady Aoi...

00:20:06.292 --> 00:20:09.083
What's with you?

00:20:10.125 --> 00:20:12.958
I don't like the look in your eyes.

00:20:18.458 --> 00:20:19.583
What the...

00:20:27.458 --> 00:20:28.792
What was that?!

00:20:30.583 --> 00:20:32.583
Boring...

00:20:34.708 --> 00:20:36.458
You all get out of here!

00:20:42.792 --> 00:20:47.292
Sealed in a tube?
That explains why I couldn't find it!

00:20:47.292 --> 00:20:51.083
In any case, that's what I need.

00:20:51.083 --> 00:20:53.750
The Eight-Hands-Breadth Sword...

00:20:55.083 --> 00:20:58.125
What do you plan to do
with the ten sacred treasures?

00:21:14.333 --> 00:21:16.083
Damn, not again...

00:21:16.083 --> 00:21:21.667
That was clothing that he gave me!

00:21:21.667 --> 00:21:25.792
All of you die!

00:21:39.333 --> 00:21:43.708
Kisaragi, you knew they'd go there.

00:21:43.708 --> 00:21:44.750
Yes.

00:21:44.750 --> 00:21:47.750
Huh?! Then you <i>knew </i>we could have been killed!

00:21:47.750 --> 00:21:49.208
Get a grip, Sakurai!

00:21:49.208 --> 00:21:50.917
But...

00:21:50.917 --> 00:21:53.333
If that had been enough to do us in,

00:21:53.333 --> 00:21:56.333
then we'd be no match for the
Demoniacal Horde, was that the idea?

00:21:56.333 --> 00:21:59.292
So, then you were testing us, huh?

00:21:59.292 --> 00:22:01.792
You've got it.

00:22:01.792 --> 00:22:03.458
Interesting.

00:22:03.458 --> 00:22:05.125
Komaki?

00:22:06.042 --> 00:22:08.958
Well, you did a good job this time.

00:22:08.958 --> 00:22:12.000
I'll treat you to dinner tonight.

00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:14.958
You said your favorite ramen shop
was around here, didn't you?

00:22:14.958 --> 00:22:18.417
Hey, now you're talking,
you Doom 'n Gloom sonnuva bitch!

00:22:18.417 --> 00:22:21.708
Okay, I'll have a large miso, butter,
kimchi, and roasted pork ramen!

00:22:21.708 --> 00:22:24.125
I won't pay for yours.

00:22:24.125 --> 00:22:25.167
You pay, damn it.

00:22:25.167 --> 00:22:26.333
I won't.

00:22:26.333 --> 00:22:27.625
Pay!

00:22:27.625 --> 00:22:28.792
Forget it!

00:22:29.667 --> 00:22:32.292
The time has come, has it?

00:22:42.250 --> 00:22:47.417
<i>I sadly hung my head a bit</i>

00:22:47.417 --> 00:22:52.500
<i>And finally you murmured</i>

00:22:52.500 --> 00:22:56.750
<i>What I heard was a faint goodbye</i>

00:22:56.750 --> 00:23:01.667
<i>Said with all your might</i>

00:23:03.625 --> 00:23:12.958
<i>Our pulses echo in the awkward silence</i>

00:23:12.958 --> 00:23:14.792
<i>We can see each other again</i>

00:23:14.792 --> 00:23:17.250
<i>Let's meet up again some time</i>

00:23:17.250 --> 00:23:23.083
<i>Let's each set out in search of our own futures</i>

00:23:23.083 --> 00:23:27.625
<i>For the kindness you gave me for my heartache</i>

00:23:27.625 --> 00:23:32.042
<i>I thank you now</i>

00:23:33.208 --> 00:23:37.833
<i>These flower petals seem just as if</i>

00:23:37.833 --> 00:23:43.458
<i>They were blessing us as we depart on our journeys</i>

00:23:43.458 --> 00:23:47.833
<i>I won't forget your warmth</i>

00:23:47.833 --> 00:23:53.125
<i>That overwhelmed my loneliness</i>

00:23:53.125 --> 00:23:58.208
<i>I thank you now</i>

